OOP - Object Oriented programming

Programing approach where we organize our program

class - BluePrint for creating objects

Object - instance of a class

OOP principles or 4 pillars of OOPS

Encapsulation - Wrapping of data(variables and methods) together and controlling access to the data
Inheritance  - one class reuse properties and methods of another class
PolyMorphism - same method can behave differently based on object
Abstraction  - Hiding unnecessary implementation details and only showing only what is neccessary

